{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778779783,"nonce":"97e9Dpa11DWqN9n63DcjvSEV4kQ=","title":"Studio bottom pane should operate on pipeline collections, not one active run","message":"## Problem\n\nThe bottom pane currently behaves too much like there is one active training run selected globally, with evaluation and analysis hanging off that selection. That does not scale to common workflows where the user trains a sweep/run set, evaluates a selected subset of runs under one protocol, then applies the same analyses across the resulting collection to produce faceted figures, summary tables, and reports.\n\nCurrent implementation has useful pieces but not the right product-level model: training runs and evaluation runs can be listed, analysis pages can store an `eval_run_id`, and figure generation exists, but the analysis generation path still discovers data by analysis module key rather than treating the selected evaluation collection as the data source.\n\n## Desired Direction\n\nKeep the current two-pane Studio layout:\n\n- Top pane: model/task/loss/structure editing.\n- Bottom pane: pipeline workspace.\n\nRepresent the lower pane as a sequence of collection transforms:\n\n1. Sweep or training plan -\u003e training run set.\n2. Evaluation protocol + selected training runs -\u003e evaluation run.\n3. Analysis definition + selected evaluation outputs -\u003e analysis run.\n4. Report assembly from analysis outputs.\n\nEach stage should default to consuming all compatible outputs from the previous stage, while allowing filters/subsets/grouping/faceting when needed.\n\n## Design Questions\n\n- Is `EvaluationRun` a batch over many training runs, rather than one child of one training run?\n- Should metrics always be represented as analysis runs, even when they are lightweight scalar summaries?\n- How should the UI expose run filters, grouping, faceting, and compatibility without forcing users to manually build Cartesian products?\n- How should reports depend on analysis outputs rather than raw training/evaluation artifacts?\n\n## Related\n\n- `93f79f2` — Studio design coordination.\n- `d90b3e5` — training runs are not distinguished from sessions/tabs.\n- `c074827` — initial two-level run selector.\n- `0cee415` — analysis page persistence.\n- `40f8322` — multi-run loss comparison.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}